{"requirements":[{"id":"filesystem_quota_datauser_srv_data","requirement":"Limit datauser to 100 MB of storage under /srv/data, enforced by the filesystem.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The executor mounted an XFS filesystem at /srv/data with user quotas enabled, configured datauser with 100M soft and hard block limits, and directly demonstrated filesystem rejection at the limit with “Disk quota exceeded.” After reboot, the account, mount, quota state, limit, and test data persisted, and a second oversized write was rejected.","evidence_ids":["cmd-2c3ae023bd1a4aa5","cmd-a6a28ba3fef14414","cmd-02339f15869a4bb2","cmd-02af972679b14372","cmd-f2a6a4d7f7c94fc5","cmd-307f3ee74bf14a0f"]}],"confidence":0.98,"operational_hygiene":{"score":0.84,"summary":"The final system was healthy: no failed services, no new listening exposure, and package health remained intact. One unnecessary troubleshooting mutation occurred: commands cmd-264823937861411f and cmd-dbd9d1348d054d58 modified the root filesystem's fstab entry and attempted to enable root quotas, but this did not contribute to the final separate-filesystem solution. The root entry was restored by cmd-90f988c7adec4048, although the safety copy /etc/fstab.pre-datauser-quota was created and no cleanup of it is recorded. The reboot protocol also left /tmp/antrieb-reboot.log, a small evidence-related residue. Quota test files and their error logs were cleaned successfully.","evidence_ids":["cmd-264823937861411f","cmd-dbd9d1348d054d58","cmd-90f988c7adec4048","cmd-307f3ee74bf14a0f","cmd-0c485d6c07ab42eb","global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:listening-sockets","global:after_executor:node1:package-health"]},"overall_summary":"The task outcome is fully satisfied with direct functional evidence. The mandatory node-restart protocol is also substantially complete: pre-restart state and boot ID were recorded, reboot was acknowledged, the boot ID changed, the system returned to running state, persistent data and quota configuration recovered, and enforcement was retested successfully. The lifecycle boot observations independently corroborate the restart.","limitations":["No final command directly inventoried /etc/fstab.pre-datauser-quota, so its apparent retention is inferred from its creation and the absence of any recorded removal in the complete command timeline.","The pre-restart evidence did not explicitly run a general system-health command, although the mounted filesystem, persistent data, and active quota enforcement were directly healthy immediately before restart."]}
